## Findings and Errors
- When opening `http://localhost:5173/` in a standard browser, the application encounters a fatal loading error before rendering the main layout.
- The UI displays:
  ```
  Something went wrong:
  Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'process')
  ```
- The console logs reveal the exact error text:
  ```
  TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'process')
      at Versions (http://localhost:5173/src/App.tsx:198:47)
      at Object.react_stack_bottom_frame (http://localhost:5173/@fs/D:/Dev/geminifinance/node_modules/.vite/deps/react-dom_client.js?v=375f47f0:18509:20)
  ```
- This error occurs because the `Versions` component in `App.tsx` tries to access `window.electron.process` which is undefined outside of an Electron preload context (i.e. inside a standard browser environment).
